%% Demo for the fuller Mermaid import (0.33.1): a Confluence-style HLD sequence diagram with every construct the importer reads.
%% Import it into a draft of sase-hld (or a blank design) with "Import Mermaid...".
%% flow: Device onboarding and first sync (from Confluence)
%% link: Confluence page https://wiki.example.com/display/SASE/Device+onboarding
%% link: Threat model https://wiki.example.com/display/SASE/Onboarding+threat+model
%% Description: A new device enrols, gets a certificate and its first policy, then syncs its posture. Frames, notes and changed steps follow the page.
sequenceDiagram
    title Device onboarding
    actor Admin as Admin console
    participant GW as onboarding-gw
    participant REG as device-registry
    participant CA as cert-authority
    participant POL as policy-engine
    participant SYNC as sync-worker
    participant AUD as audit-trail

    Admin->>GW: POST /devices: enrol a new device
    Note over GW: the gateway rate-limits enrolments per tenant
    %% real: http:POST device-registry/v2/devices
    GW->>REG: POST /devices: register the device
    REG->>REG: validate serial number
    alt device is known
        REG-->>GW: existing device
    else device is new
        REG->>CA: POST /certificates: issue a device certificate
        CA-->>REG: certificate
        Note over REG,CA: the certificate is valid for 90 days
        REG-->>GW: registered
    end
    Note right of GW: enrolment is acknowledged to the console
    GW-->>Admin: 201 enrolled

    rect rgb(255, 244, 214)
        GW->>POL: GET /policies/default: fetch the first policy %% real: http:GET policy-engine/policies/{tenantId}/default
        Note over GW,POL: new in v2: the policy is signed
        POL->>POL: sign policy bundle
    end

    loop for each pending sync batch
        opt batch is not empty
            GW-)SYNC: Sync: queue the batch
            par audit the batch
                SYNC->>AUD: POST /events: batch received
                Note left of AUD: the audit trail keeps the events for a year
            and verify the batch
                SYNC->>POL: POST /verify: check the posture rules
                critical certificate is valid
                    SYNC->>CA: GET /certificates/{id}: check the revocation list
                option certificate is revoked
                    SYNC->>AUD: POST /events: revoked certificate used
                end
            end
            break batch is rejected
                SYNC->>AUD: POST /events: batch rejected
            end
        end
    end
